1 The present criminal revision has been filed to quash the order dated 08.07.2024 passed by the Court of Additional Sessions Judge / Special Judge, POCSO Act, Court No. 1, Gorakhpur in Criminal Appeal No. 68 of 2024 and the order dated 06.05.2024 passed by the Principal Magistrate, Juvenile Justice Board, Gorakhpur in Case Crime No. 52 of 2024 (State vs. Sundaram) under Sections- 363,
366, 504, 376 IPC and Section 5/6 of POCSO Act, Police Station- Bansgaon, District- Gorakhpur.
Learned counsel for the revisionist submits:
(i) admittedly, the revisionist was a juvenile on the date of alleged incident being 12 years, 09 months and 01 days of age; he is in child protection home since 20.02.2024.
(ii) the revisionist has been falsely implicated;
(iii) there is no specific or strong objection raised in the DPO report, other than the general and vague observations;
(iv) there is no criminal history of the revisionist;
(v) there is no hope of early conclusion of the trial;
(vi) the revisionist has remained confined in the child observation home for an unduly long period of time;
(vii) none of the grounds contemplated under section 12 of the Juvenile Justice (Care and Protection of Children) Act, 2000 (hereinafter referred to as the Act) are available, to deny the bail to the revisionist.
